Sure, I'll provide a complete example of a Minecraft Fabric Mod that adds an Emerald Sword with custom damage. We'll include a custom `EmeraldDamageableEntity` class to handle the damage calculation and a `CustomEmeraldSword` class to define the Emerald Sword.

### Step 1: Create the mod structure

Create a directory structure like this:

```
fabric-emerald-sword
├── build.gradle
├── fabric-plugin.gradle
├── src
│   └── main
│       └── java
